## Start a Singularity shell

Use this to run `spack` commands interactively inside the container with the same bind mounts as the batch jobs:

```bash
singularity shell \
  --bind "{{ script_dir }}:{{ script_dir }}" \
  --bind "{{ repo_dir }}:{{ repo_dir }}" \
  --bind "{{ outputs_dir }}:{{ outputs_dir }}" \
  --bind "{{ spack_user_config_path }}:{{ spack_user_config_path }}" \
  "{{ sif_path }}"
```

Inside the shell, ensure Spack uses the generated per-user config:

```bash
export SPACK_USER_CONFIG_PATH="{{ spack_user_config_path }}"
```

## Example spack commands

Check versions:

```bash
{{ spack_in_container }} --version
```

If `environment_name` was provided to `setup.py`, use it with `-e`:

```bash
{% if environment_name %}
{{ spack_in_container }} -e "{{ environment_name }}" env status
{{ spack_in_container }} -e "{{ environment_name }}" install <spec>
{% else %}
{{ spack_in_container }} install <spec>
{% endif %}
```

